# {{.Name}}

This independent Go module is {{.Module}}. It requires Go {{.GoVersion}} or later
and pins Fathomry to {{.FrameworkVersion}}. The selected template uses the existing
public CLI shell; shared usage text still says fathomry. It is not a Worker,
workflow executor, configuration loader or initialized deployment.

## Resolve dependencies explicitly

Generation did not run Go, Git or service checks. Resolve dependencies yourself:

```sh
GOWORK=off go mod tidy
GOWORK=off go test ./...
GOWORK=off go run ./cmd/{{.Name}} --help
```

Go creates go.sum and may add indirect requirements. Keep those files with your
project. No local replacement, parent workspace or copied SDK tree is required
for this qualified CLI profile. This does not qualify every future Adapter.

## Build and run

Set BUILD_OUTPUT to an existing directory you own. Use a temporary-build area for
disposable experiments and a permanent artifact location for retained binaries.

```sh
test -n "$BUILD_OUTPUT" && test -d "$BUILD_OUTPUT" &&
  GOWORK=off go build -o "$BUILD_OUTPUT/{{.Name}}" ./cmd/{{.Name}}
"$BUILD_OUTPUT/{{.Name}}" --help
```

The binary embeds the CLI; it does not invoke a globally installed fathomry or
require Go/the original source directory at runtime. The binary owns application
exit codes; go run can wrap a failed program's exit status.

## Ownership and current limits

The generated files are project-owned and may be edited. Future template changes
do not overwrite them. No automatic updater, service discovery, registration,
database migration, workflow/Mode definition or deployment was generated.
The config directory currently contains documentation only.

The developer-only project-new command is not part of this project's public CLI
shell. Build the official developer CLI from its supported source checkout;
versioned go install of the supplying Fathomry module currently rejects its local
replacement directives. Do not copy that replacement graph into this module.

Template notices describe the supplied source. No business-owner identity or
project-wide business license was selected on your behalf.
